Job Number: 50028
Department: Education Bureau
Division/Section/Unit: Higher Education Division
Job Title: Executive Manager (Education Hub) (EDB/HE/127/26 )
Salary: $58,890 per month
Entry Requirements: (a) A Hong Kong bachelor's degree, or equivalent [see Notes (ii) & (iii)];
(b) Met the language proficiency requirements of Level 3 or above in Chinese Language and English Language in the Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education Examination (HKDSEE) or the Hong Kong Certificate of Education Examination (HKCEE), or equivalent [see Note (v)];
(c) At least 6 years of full-time post-degree working experience (of which at least 4 years in administration and management work);
(d) Working experience in tender process in the government/public sector or publicity and marketing preferred;
(e) Self-motivated, able to work under pressure and can handle multiple projects within tight timeframe;
(f) Strong planning, organization and analytical skills;
(g) Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills;
(h) Excellent command of both written and spoken English and Chinese, fluent in Putonghua; and
(i) Familiar with computer operations, such as word processing, spreadsheet and presentation software.
[ Remarks : This post is open to male and female applicants. ]
Note: (i) For general awareness, a locally-accredited Hong Kong bachelor's degree is at Level 5 under the Hong Kong Qualifications Framework (HKQF). While there are other qualifications under HKQF Level 5, for the purpose of this recruitment exercise, only bachelor's degree is acceptable. Further information on HKQF may be accessed on HKQF's website (https://www.hkqf.gov.hk) or by phone (3793 3955).
(ii) Candidates should mark clearly on their application forms the major and minor subjects studied in their degree courses. Candidates possessing additional qualifications (e.g. a second/higher degree in a relevant subject) should include details in their application forms.
(iii) For qualifications awarded by local institutions/Hong Kong Examinations and Assessment Authority, copies of the relevant transcripts/diplomas/certificates/other qualification documents are not required to be submitted at this stage of application. For qualifications obtained from institutions outside Hong Kong, copies of the relevant transcripts/diplomas/certificates or other qualification documents should be submitted. Applicants with qualifications obtained from institutions outside Hong Kong, they should submit copies of the required documents by email to enquiry_ncr@edb.gov.hk on or before 21 May 2026 (the receipt date on the email will be regarded as the date of submission). The on-line application number should be quoted in the email and on the copies of the supporting documents. If candidates fail to provide the supporting documents as required, their applications will not be considered.
(iv) For appointment purpose, "Grade C" in Chinese Language and English Language (Syllabus B) in HKCEE before 2007 are accepted administratively as comparable to "Level 3" in Chinese Language and English Language in the 2007 HKCEE and henceforth.
(v) Candidates should state the nature and relevancy of the post-degree experience.
(vi) As invitations or notifications will be sent to candidates by email, candidates should provide an accurate email address in their application. Candidates are responsible for checking their emails to ensure that invitation(s) or notification(s) will be duly received.
Duties: (a) To provide secretariat and administrative support to projects related to the development of the Northern Metropolis University Town and strengthening Hong Kong's position as an International Education Hub;
(b) To arrange meetings, consultation sessions and site visits/field trips;
(c) To support the planning and implementation of large-scale publicity campaign;
(d) To compile reports on project development and progress;
(e) To perform administrative and budget monitoring duties; and
(f) To formulate replies to enquiries from the public, press and Legislative Council Members.
Terms of Appointment: Successful candidates will be employed on non-civil service contract terms for 1 year.
Fringe Benefits (a) 14 days annual leave and full pay sickness allowance whereas rest days, statutory holidays(or substituted holidays), maternity leave / paternity leave, where appropriate, will be granted in accordance with the provisions of the Employment Ordinance.
(b) A gratuity may be granted upon satisfactory completion of the contract with consistently high standard of performance and conduct. Such gratuity, if granted, plus any contribution made by the Government to a Mandatory Provident Fund (MPF) scheme in respect of the appointee as required by the MPF Schemes Ordinance, will be equal to 10% of the total basic salary drawn during the contract period.
