Job Number: 49994
Department: Information Services Department
Job Title: English Language Writer / Assistant Editor (English)
Salary: HK$101,775 per month for English Language Writer
HK$82,330 per month for Assistant Editor (English)
Entry Requirements: The Information Services Department (ISD) is conducting a joint recruitment for the positions of (i) English Language Writer, and (ii) Assistant Editor (English). Applicants may apply for either or both positions. Eligible candidates will be invited to attend a joint recruitment written test conducted by ISD in Hong Kong, aiming to assess their proficiency in English writing and editing. Only those who have passed the written test will be further considered. Selected candidates will be invited to attend the individual interviews for the respective posts.

English Language Writer

Applicants should –

(1) have a Hong Kong bachelor’s degree or equivalent, preferably majoring in a relevant subject of Journalism, Media/Communication Studies, Cultural Studies, Humanities, Languages, or equivalent;
(2) have at least ten years of relevant work experience [Note] in English writing, in particular op-ed, speech and social media post writing;
(3) have good editing and communication skills;
(4) have a very good understanding of current affairs, both locally and outside Hong Kong;
(5) be prepared to work outside normal office hours and meet tight deadlines; and
(6) be computer-literate, with good English word processing skills.

Assistant Editor (English)

Applicants should –

(1) have a Hong Kong bachelor’s degree or equivalent, preferably majoring in a relevant subject of Journalism, Media/Communication Studies, Film/Television Studies, Cultural Studies, Humanities, Languages, or equivalent;
(2) have at least eight years of relevant work experience [Note] in journalism (English media) or equivalent, preferably with experience in news reporting/broadcasting and web publishing/social media;
(3) be proficient in English speaking and news writing, and have good editing and communication skills;
(4) be familiar with news video production, including reporting, script writing and voice-over work;
(5) be prepared to work outside normal office hours and meet tight deadlines; and
(6) be computer-literate, with good English word processing skills.
